{
  "conformance_version": "1.4.0",
  "file": "b8-fixtures",
  "contract": "b8/1.1",
  "contract_note": "b8/1 plus one additive rule (rules.context: webhook_context values are valid Unicode and finite) and three clarifications that change no b8/1 answer: strict UTF-8 and RFC 8259 at parse, the exact protocol rule, and the canonical measure of the 1,024-byte rule",
  "schema": "schemas/b8/notice.v1.schema.json",
  "order": "parse (invalid_field ''), protocol major and event known (else 503 protocol_unsupported), identity deny list (identity_not_allowed), context values (b8/1.1, invalid_field run.webhook_context), schema (invalid_field with the failing path), semantic rules in contract order; each fixture names its step",
  "steps": [
    "parse",
    "protocol",
    "identity",
    "context",
    "schema",
    "semantic",
    "accepted"
  ],
  "rules": {
    "parse": "Decode the body as strict UTF-8 (no BOM, no invalid byte, no encoded surrogate; never substitute U+FFFD) and parse it as RFC 8259 JSON (no NaN, Infinity or -Infinity literal). Failure, or a value that is not an object: 400 invalid_field, field ''.",
    "protocol": "503 protocol_unsupported (EE: 503 relay_unavailable, reason protocol_unsupported) when either protocol is a JSON string matching ^omega-deploy-run-event/v([1-9][0-9]*)$ whose major is not 1, or event is a JSON string other than run.completed and run.failed. Nothing else answers 503: an absent protocol, one that is not a string, or any other text (omega-deploy-run-event/v01, /v1.1, 'v1 ') goes on to the schema, which answers 400 invalid_field 'protocol'; likewise an event that is absent or not a string gives 'event'.",
    "identity": "the deny list: top level deployment, organization_id, workspace_id, project_id, relay, then in run deployment_id, organization_id, workspace_id, project_id; the first present, in that order, is the field of 400 identity_not_allowed.",
    "context": "b8/1.1, checked before the schema so the answer does not depend on a validator's number handling (Ajv's default strictNumbers refuses Infinity inside the schema step): when run is an object and run.webhook_context is an object, a key or string value holding a lone surrogate (a \\ud800-\\udfff escape not part of a pair), or a number value that is not finite (1e400 parses to Infinity), is 400 invalid_field 'run.webhook_context'.",
    "schema": "notice.v1.schema.json. field is the path of the failing value, dot-joined (for a required failure the missing key is appended; inside a oneOf, the value that fails). field is normative only when the notice has exactly one schema error, as every fixture here has: with several, jsonschema's best_match and Ajv may name different ones, and EE and FA may differ.",
    "semantic": "in contract order: event_status_mismatch (field event); run.error null iff succeeded; created_at <= started_at <= ended_at when started_at is set and created_at <= ended_at always, reporting the later field; run.webhook in URL form with no userinfo and no fragment; run.webhook_context at most 1,024 bytes, measured as the UTF-8 length of the context written by the canonical serializer of payloads.json (JSON.stringify: raw UTF-8, never \\u escapes; numbers as ECMAScript writes them). Not Python's json.dumps, not characters or UTF-16 units.",
    "accepted": "202 with the answer of accepted.v1.schema.json."
  },
